From 94a4a69eb811e673adcd0816107e82cbb3a81a05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kshot3000 <kshot9000@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:22:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: target overflow fail-closed, strict --pool parsing, CPU
 align-test, config sync, docs, vendored tree-size check

B1 (HIGH): difficulty-fallback share target was 2^32x too easy and saturated
to U256::MAX on overflow, so every tile 'beat' the target and all submitted
shares were pool-invalid. cp_target_from_difficulty now subtracts the jackpot
scale factor in the exponent (bound = 2^(256-d) exactly); cp_scale_target_le /
cp_scale_jackpot_target return 0 and zero the bound on 256-bit overflow
(fail-closed, mirroring upstream pearl penalized_target_bound); all CPU/CUDA/
OpenCL scan call sites skip the job loudly on overflow.

B2 (MEDIUM): --pool with a malformed URI (missing scheme/host) or invalid port
was silently ignored, mining to the default pool. Now errors and exits(1).

B3 (LOW): --align-test refused on CPU-only builds though the tests are pure
CPU (keyed-BLAKE3 noise, Merkle chunk roots, V3 salted-seed pinned vectors).
Now runs on CPU builds; GPU self-tests skipped when no GPU backend.

B4 (LOW): scripts/plain_proof_host.py mining-config blobs encoded stale
k=4096/rank=256; regenerated byte-identical to src/common/cp_noise.c
(k=2048/rank=128).

B5 (LOW): docs/hashrate_calculation.md overstated per-tile work 2x (524,288
vs actual 262,144 MACs); docs/proof.md corrected to M=131072/N=262144/k=2048/
rank=128 and now documents V3 salted-seed certificates.

B6 (LOW): vendored third_party/zk-pow omitted upstream's
check_declared_tree_sizes; ported verbatim from pearl-research-labs/pearl and
wired into parse_proof.
